          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            Subsets
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            of a set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            correspond precisely to maps from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            to the set of truth values of classical logic via their
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/characteristic+function"} characteristic function
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi χ
                      %mi A
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \chi_A:X\to \{0,1\}
            %strong subobject classifier
            generalizes this situation to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/toposes"} toposes
            other than
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
          %p
            A
            %em subobject classifier
            in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
            is a morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi true
                  %mo :
                  %mo *
                  %mo →
                  %mi Ω
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} true : * \to \Omega
            such that every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monomorphism"} monomorphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \hookrightarrow B
            in the topos (hence every
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subobject"} subobject
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
            of this morphism along a unique morphism (the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/characteristic+morphism"} characteristic morphism
            of
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %mo →
                    %mi Ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B \to \Omega
          %p
            In this sense
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ω
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classifying+space"} classifying object
            for subobjects and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi true
                  %mo :
                  %mo *
                  %mo →
                  %mi Ω
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} true : * \to \Omega
            the
            %em generic
            subobject.
          %p
            The existence of a subobject classifier in a category is a powerful property which induces much other structure that lies at the heart of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos+theory"} topos theory
          %p
            By restricting the class of monomorphism appropriately, the concept can be relativized to the concept of an
            %em
              %strong> M
              \-subobject classifier
            = succeed ":" do
              %sup#fnref:1
                %a{:href => "#fn:1", :rel => "footnote"} 1
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasitopos"} quasitoposes
          %p
            In
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+theory"} type theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type"} type
            closely related to the subobject classifier is the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+of+propositions"} type of propositions
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Prop
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Prop
            or (sometimes in
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+theory"} homotopy type theory
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi hProp
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} hProp
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
          #DefinitionOfSubobjectClassifier.num_defn
            %h6 Definition
            %p
            %p
              In a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              with
              = succeed "s," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+limit"} finite limit
              %strong subobject classifier
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monomorphism"} monomorphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi true
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo *
                    %mo →
                    %mi Ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} true \,\colon\, * \to \Omega
              out of the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object"} terminal object
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monomorphism"} monomorphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \to X
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              there is a unique
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi χ
                      %mi U
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \chi_U \colon X \to \Omega
              such that the following
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+square"} square commutes
              and is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+square"} Cartesian
              (a
              = succeed "):" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi U
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mo *
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ↓
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mrow
                                  %mrow
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                    %mi pb
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ↓
                            %mrow
                              %msup
                                %mrow
                                %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                  %mi true
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi χ
                                  %mi U
                          %mtd
                            %mi Ω
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mrow
                                %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                                %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    U &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; *
                    \\\
                    \\big\downarrow
                    \&amp;{}^{{}_{(pb)}}&amp;
                    \\big\downarrow{{}^\mathrlap{true}}
                    \\\
                    X &amp;\underset{\chi_U}{\longrightarrow}&amp; \Omega
                    \\mathrlap{\,.}
                    }
            %p
          %p
            See for instance (
            %a{:href => "#MacLaneMoerdijk"}> MacLane-Moerdijk, p. 32
            ).
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p Some terminology:
            %p
              If it exists, the object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega
              is also called the
              = succeed "," do
                %strong
                  object of
                  = succeed "s" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/truth+value"} truth value
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+element"} global element
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mo →
                    %mi Ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K \to \Omega
              is called a
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/truth+value"} truth value
              and the element
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi true
                    %mo :
                    %mo *
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi Ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} true : * \hookrightarrow \Omega
              is the truth value
              = succeed "," do
                %strong
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/true"} true
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+logic"} internal logic
              of the category
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %p
              Note that the subobjects classified by the truth values are
              = succeed "s." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subterminal+object"} subterminal object
            %p
              The morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi χ
                      %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \chi_U
              is also called the
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/characteristic+map"} characteristic map
              or
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classifying+map"} classifying map
              of the subobject
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                      %mo ↪
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \hookrightarrow X
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              has
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+limit"} finite limit
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+small+category"} locally small category
              = succeed "-assigning" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subobject"} subobject
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf"} presheaf
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Sub
                    %mo :
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mi op
                    %mo →
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Sub : C^{op} \to Set
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ↦
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi U
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo ∼
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    X \mapsto \{U \hookrightarrow X\}/\sim
            %p
              is
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representable+functor"} representable
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+the"} the
              subobject classifier: there is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+isomorphism"} natural isomorphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Sub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Sub(X) \simeq C(X, \Omega)
            %p
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in C
            %p
              Moreover, in this case
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              is
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/well-powered+category"} well powered
          %p
            This appears for instance as (
            %a{:href => "#MacLaneMoerdijk"}> MacLane-Moerdijk, prop. I.3.1
            ).
          %p
            In more detail: given a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi c
                  %mo →
                  %mi d
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f: c \to d
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Sub
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi Sub
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi d
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi Sub
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi c
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Sub(f): Sub(d) \to Sub(c)
          %p
            takes a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subobject"} subobject
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi i
                  %mo :
                  %mi t
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi d
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i: t \hookrightarrow d
            to the subobject of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi c
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c
            obtained by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pulling back
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
            along
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            = succeed "s," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monomorphism"} monomorphism
          %p
            The representability of this functor means there is an object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ω
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega
            together with a subobject
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi t
                  %mo :
                  %mi T
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi Ω
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t: T \hookrightarrow \Omega
            which is
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+construction"} universal
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                    %mo :
                    %mi s
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i: s \hookrightarrow c
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi c
                  %mo →
                  %mi Ω
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f: c \to \Omega
            such that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
            is obtained as the pullback of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi t
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t
            along
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              To see that a subobject classifier induces such a natural isomorphism, we need that the morphisms
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Sub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sub(f)
              for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Mor
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \in Mor(C)
              corresponds to the morphisms
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi f
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Ω
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C(f,\Omega)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pasting+law"} pasting law
              for
              = succeed "s." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
            %p
              Conversely, to see that a subobjects-representing object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega
              is a subobject classifier, use that by
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} naturality
              we have for each morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi : X \to \Omega
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+diagram"} commuting diagram
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi Sub
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi Ω
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mo ≃
                          %mtd
                            %mi C
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi Ω
                            %mo ,
                            %mi Ω
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mi Sub
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %mi ϕ
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mi C
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %mi ϕ
                                  %mo ,
                                  %mi Ω
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi Sub
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mo ≃
                          %mtd
                            %mi C
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo ,
                            %mi Ω
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    Sub(\Omega) &amp;\stackrel{\simeq}{\to}&amp; C(\Omega, \Omega)
                    \\\
                    {}^{\mathllap{Sub(\phi)}}\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{C(\phi,\Omega)}}
                    \\\
                    Sub(X) &amp;\stackrel{\simeq}{\to}&amp; C(X, \Omega)
                    }
            %p
              whose commutativity says that every element of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Sub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sub(X)
              is the pullback along some
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi : X \to \Omega
              of the subobject of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega
              corresponding under the natural isomorphism to
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Id
                      %mo :
                      %mi Ω
                      %mo →
                      %mi Ω
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Id : \Omega \to \Omega
            %p
              By further playing around with this one finds that this latter subobject of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega
              has to be a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object"} terminal object
          %h2#examples Examples
          %h3#in_
            In
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
          %p
            In the category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sets"} Sets
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sets"} sets
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mn 2
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi f
                  %mo ,
                  %mi t
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{2} = \{f, t\}
            (the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+mathematics"} classical
            = succeed ")" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Boolean+domain"} Boolean domain
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi t
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mn 1
                  %mo →
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t \colon  1 \to \mathbf{2}
            just names the element
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi t
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subset"} subset
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mo ⊆
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \subseteq X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi χ
                    %mi S
                  %mo :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \chi_S: X \to \mathbf{2}
            is the function defined by
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi χ
                    %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi t
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \chi_S(x) = t
            if
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in S
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi χ
                    %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \chi_S(x) = f
            if
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∉
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \notin S
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_2 Remark
            %p
              It is not usually true in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/toposes"} toposes
              that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproduct"} coproduct
              = succeed ";" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mn 2
                      %mo =
                      %mn 1
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{2} = 1 + 1
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Boolean+topos"}> Boolean
                \. Thus the category
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Set
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
                of sets is a Boolean topos, as is the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf"} presheaf
                topos
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi Set
                        %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set^G
                when
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                is a
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid"} groupoid
          %h3#in_a_presheaf_topos In a presheaf topos
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              The subobject classifier in a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf+topos"} presheaf topos
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PSh(S)
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf"} presheaf
              that sends each
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \in S
              to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi sieves
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sieves(U)
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sieves"} sieves
              on it
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ω
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi U
                    %mo ↦
                    %mi sieves
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Omega
                    \\;\colon\;
                    U \mapsto sieves(U)
            %p
              Here
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi sieves
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sieves(U)
              is equivalently the set of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subobjects"} subobjects
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representable+functor"} representable
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf"} presheaf
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y(U)
            %p
              The corresponding morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi true
                    %mo :
                    %mo *
                    %mo →
                    %mi Ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} true : * \to \Omega
              of presheaves is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} natural transformation
              that picks over each object the
              %em maximal sieve
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi true
                        %mi U
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mi maximal
                        %mrow
                          %mi sieves
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi U
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo :
                      %mo *
                      %mo →
                      %mi sieves
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} true_U = maximal_{sieves(U)} : * \to sieves(U)
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_3 Remark
            %p
              If one views a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf"} presheaf
              over a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"} small category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              as a set varying (or evolving) over
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PSh(S)
              may be viewed as encapsulating the ways of an element to be in the set ranging from ‘never’ to ‘always’ being in the set.
            %p
              In
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Set
                    %mo =
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set = PSh(\ast)
              these two extremes are the only possibilities, but in the general case there are ways to become an element ‘over time’.
            %p
              It might be helpful to have a look at the simple example of a subobject classifier in the presheaf topos of directed graphs worked out at
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quiv"} Quiv
              to get some intuition.
          %h4#in__2
            In
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G Set
          %p
            As a special case of presheaf toposes, for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+group"} discrete group
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                  %mi Set
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Set
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G Set = [\mathbf{B} G, Set]
            the topos of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G-sets"} G-sets
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sieves"} sieves
            on the single object of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping"} delooping
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid"} groupoid
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
            = succeed "-set" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
          %p
            For toposes of (left) actions of general
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid"} monoids
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            the picture changes dramatically, since then there will usually exist non-trivial left ideals and, accordingly, the structure of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ω
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega
            will become richer: Its underlying set has elements all left ideals, with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi m
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m\in M
            acting on a left ideal
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            by mapping it to the left ideal
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi n
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi M
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi n
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi m
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi L
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{n\in M| n\cdot m\in L\}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ω
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega
            applies to the case of groups as well, it is just, that groups lack non-trivial left ideals!)
          %h3#in_a_sheaf_topos In a sheaf topos
          %p
            The following is adapted from p. 34 of
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Caramello"} Caramello
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo ,
                  %mi J
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (C, J)
            be a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} Grothendieck site
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sieve"} sieve
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            on an object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi c
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c \in C
            is
            = succeed "-closed" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi J
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi d
                    %mo →
                    %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f :d \to c
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi J
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi d
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^*(S) \in J(d)
            then
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \in S
            %em closed
            since this is a closure property:
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            contains all arrows it covers. If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo ,
                  %mi J
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (C, J)
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locale"} locale
            with the open covers topology, then this condition means that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            is a collection of subopens of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi c
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c
            which is closed under unions. Clearly, every sieve on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi c
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c
            can be saturated to a closed one.
          %p
            The subobject classifier of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Sh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo ,
                  %mi J
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Sh}(C,J)
            is defined on objects as
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Ω
                    %mi J
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi c
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mtext S is a J-closed sieve on c
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Omega_J(c) = \{ S | \text{S is a J-closed sieve on c} \}
          %p and on morphisms as
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Ω
                    %mi J
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi c
                  %mo →
                  %mi d
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Omega_J(f : c \to d) = f^*
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^*
            denotes, as above, pullback of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sieve"} sieves
          %p
            The arrow
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "sans-serif"}
                    %mi true
                  %mo :
                  %mn 1
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi Ω
                    %mi J
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathsf{true} : 1 \to \Omega_J
            picks the maximal sieve on each object (the one generated by the identity).
          %p
            Given a mono
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi m
                    %mo :
                    %mi B
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m : B \to A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi χ
                    %mi m
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi Ω
                    %mi J
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \chi_m : A \to \Omega_J
            is given by
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi χ
                    %mi m
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi c
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi d
                  %mo →
                  %mi c
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi d
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\chi_m(c)(x) = \{f : d \to c | A(f)(x) \in B(d)\},
          %p
            for any
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi c
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c \in C
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in A(c)
          %h3#in_a_nonboolean_topos In a non-boolean topos
          %p
            An example of a non-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Boolean+topos"} Boolean topos
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+sheaves"} category of sheaves
            over a “typical”
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            such as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+line"} real line
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℝ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
            in its usual
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topology"} topology
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ω
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega
            is the sheaf where the set of sections over an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+subset"} open subset
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            is the set of open subsets of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf+and+topos+theory"} sheaf topos
            in this case is guaranteed to be non-Boolean provided there are some non-regular open sets in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            (a open set is
            %em regular
            if it is the interior of its closure). The “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+logic"}> internal logic
            ” of such a topos is
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intuitionistic+logic"} intuitionistic
          %h3#in_a_slice_topos In a slice topos
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℰ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℰ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in \mathcal{E}
              any object. Write
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℰ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}/X
              for the corresponding
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/over-topos"} over-topos
            %p
              The subobject classifier of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℰ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}/X
              is
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi p
                        %mn 2
                      %mo :
                      %msub
                        %mi Ω
                        %mi ℰ
                      %mo ×
                      %mi X
                      %mo →
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p_2 : \Omega_{\mathcal{E}} \times X \to X
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p
              This follows for instance from the statement that the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inverse+image"} inverse image
              of any
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/base+change+geometric+morphism"} base change geometric morphism
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/logical+functor"} logical functor
              and hence preserves subobject classifiers: Here we are looking at the base change along
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p : X \to *
              and hence
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi p
                        %mo *
                      %msub
                        %mi Ω
                        %mi ℰ
                      %mo ≃
                      %msub
                        %mi Ω
                        %mi ℰ
                      %mo ×
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p^* \Omega_{\mathcal{E}}\simeq \Omega_{\mathcal{E}} \times X
            %p But the statement is also easily directly checked.
          %h3#in_a_nontopos In a non-topos
          %p
            The category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Set
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set_\ast
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+sets"} pointed sets
            has a subobject classifier (specified up to unique isomorphism as the pointed set with two elements).
          %p
            If one is willing to admit non-locally small categories, then the category of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proper+class"} classes
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ZFC"} ZFC
            is not a topos (it is not cartesian closed) but has a subobject classifier: any two-element set.
          %p
            The opposite of the category of commutative von Neumann algebras has a subobject classifier given by
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℂ
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}^2
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "https://mathoverflow.net/questions/384346/is-the-opposite-category-of-commutative-von-neumann-algebras-a-topos"} according to Simon Henry on MathOverflow
          %h2#properties Properties
          %p
            Suppose a category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{C}
            has a subobject classifier; this entails some striking structural consequences for
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{C}
          #regular.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_4 Proposition
            %p
              Every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monomorphism"} monomorphism
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{C}
              is a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+monomorphism"} regular monomorphism
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equalizer"} equalizer
              of some pair of maps.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_3 Proof
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi χ
                      %mi i
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \chi_i: X \to \Omega
              the characteristic map of a mono
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo →
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i: A \to X
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
              is the equalizer of a pair of maps
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo ⇉
                      %mi Ω
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \rightrightarrows \Omega
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mn 1
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                              %mo !
                            %mo ↗
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mi t
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi χ
                                  %mi i
                          %mtd
                            %mi Ω
                            %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \&amp; &amp; 1 \\
                    \&amp; \mathllap{!} \nearrow &amp; \downarrow \mathrlap{t} \\
                    X &amp; \underset{\chi_i}{\to} &amp; \Omega.
                    }
          .num_cor
            %h6#corollary Corollary
            %p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{C}
              is
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/balanced+category"} balanced
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{C}
              is an isomorphism iff it is both
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monomorphism"} monic
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/epimorphism"} epic
          .proof
            %h6#proof_4 Proof
            %p
              “Only if” is trivial. The “if” comes from the fact that an epic (epimorphic) equalizer must be an isomorphism, for if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i: A \to X
              is the equalizer of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo ,
                    %mi g
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo ⇉
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f, g: X \rightrightarrows Y
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
              is epic, then
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo =
                      %mi g
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f = g
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mn 1
                      %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1_X
              is their equalizer, so
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i: A \to X
              must have been an isomorphism.
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_5 Proposition
            %p
              Any two epi-mono factorizations of a map in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{C}
              are canonically isomorphic.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_5 Proof
            %p
              Suppose
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                    %mi p
                    %mo =
                    %mi j
                    %mi q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i p = j q
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo ,
                    %mi q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p, q
              are epic and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                    %mo ,
                    %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i, j
              are monic. Since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j
              is regular, it is the equalizer of some parallel pair
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo ,
                    %mi g
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f, g
              as in the diagram
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi p
                          %mtd
                            %mi B
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                              %mi q
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mi i
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi C
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo →
                              %mi j
                          %mtd
                            %mi D
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %munder
                                %mo →
                                %mi g
                              %mover
                                %mo →
                                %mi f
                          %mtd
                            %mi E
                            %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    A &amp; \stackrel{p}{\to} &amp; B &amp; &amp; \\
                    \\mathllap{q} \downarrow &amp; &amp; \downarrow \mathrlap{i} &amp; &amp; \\
                    C &amp; \underset{j}{\to} &amp; D &amp; \stackrel{\overset{f}{\to}}{\underset{g}{\to}} &amp; E,
                    }
            %p
              so that
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mi i
                      %mi p
                      %mo =
                      %mi f
                      %mi j
                      %mi q
                      %mo =
                      %mi g
                      %mi j
                      %mi q
                      %mo =
                      %mi g
                      %mi i
                      %mi p
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f i p = f j q = g j q = g i p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mi i
                    %mo =
                    %mi g
                    %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f i = g i
              since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              is epic, whence
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
              factors through
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j
              as
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j
              is the equalizer:
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                    %mo =
                    %mi j
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i = j k
              for some
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                      %mo :
                      %mi B
                      %mo →
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k: B \to C
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                    %mi p
                    %mo =
                    %mi q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k p = q
              since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi j
                    %mi k
                    %mi p
                    %mo =
                    %mi i
                    %mi p
                    %mo =
                    %mi j
                    %mi q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j k p = i p = j q
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j
              is monic. We have that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              is monic since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
              is, and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              is epic since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q
              is. Thus
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              is an isomorphism.
          %p
            Already these results impose some tight restrictions on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{C}
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega
          %p
            The subobject classifier always comes with the structure of an internal
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partial+order"} poset
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ⊆
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi Ω
                  %mo ×
                  %mi Ω
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \subseteq\, \hookrightarrow \Omega\times\Omega
            which is internally reflexive, antisymmetric, and transitive. This can be constructed directly (see Proposition
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#implication"}
            below), or obtained via the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+lemma"} Yoneda lemma
            since the collection of subobjects of any object is an external poset.
          %p
            Similarly, since we assume that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{C}
            is finitely complete, each subobject poset
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Sub
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sub(X)
            has intersections (gotten as pullbacks or
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+products"} fiber products
            of pairs of monics
            = succeed ")," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi j
                    %mo :
                    %mi B
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i: A \to X,j: B \to X
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∩
                  %mo :
                  %mi Sub
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ×
                  %mi Sub
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi Sub
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \cap: Sub(X) \times Sub(X) \to Sub(X)
          %p
            is natural in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∩
                  %mo :
                  %mi hom
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Ω
                  %mo ×
                  %mi Ω
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi hom
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Ω
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \cap: \hom(X, \Omega \times \Omega) \to \hom(X, \Omega)
          %p
            natural in
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+lemma"} Yoneda lemma
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∧
                  %mo :
                  %mi Ω
                  %mo ×
                  %mi Ω
                  %mo →
                  %mi Ω
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \wedge: \Omega \times \Omega \to \Omega
          %p
            making
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ω
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega
            an internal
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/meet-semilattice"} meet-semilattice
          %p
            More significantly,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ω
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega
            is an internal
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Heyting+algebra"} Heyting algebra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+closed+category"} cartesian closed
            poset:
          #implication.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_6 Proposition
            %p There is an internal implication operator
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ⇒
                    %mo :
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo ×
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo →
                    %mi Ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Rightarrow: \Omega \times \Omega \to \Omega
            %p uniquely specified by the internal condition
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi w
                    %mo ∧
                    %mi u
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi v
                    %mspace{:width => "2em"}
                    %mi iff
                    %mspace{:width => "2em"}
                    %mi w
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi u
                    %mo ⇒
                    %mi v
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w \wedge u \leq v \qquad iff \qquad w \leq u \Rightarrow v.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_sketch Proof (sketch)
            %p
              Construct
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ⊆
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo ×
                    %mi Ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \subseteq \hookrightarrow \Omega \times \Omega
              as the equalizer of the pair of maps
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo ×
                    %mi Ω
                    %mover
                      %munder
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mo ∧
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi π
                            %mn 1
                    %mi Ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega \times \Omega \stackrel{\overset{\pi_1}{\longrightarrow}}{\underset{\wedge}{\longrightarrow}} \Omega
            %p
              and then define
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ⇒
                    %mo :
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo ×
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo →
                    %mi Ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Rightarrow: \Omega \times \Omega \to \Omega
              to be the characteristic map of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ⊆
                      %mo ↪
                      %mi Ω
                      %mo ×
                      %mi Ω
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \subseteq \hookrightarrow \Omega \times \Omega
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi χ
                      %mi u
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi χ
                      %mi v
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \chi_u, \chi_v
              are two maps
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo →
                      %mi Ω
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to \Omega
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi w
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w \hookrightarrow X
              is contained in the subobject classified by
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi χ
                      %mi u
                    %mo ⇒
                    %msub
                      %mi χ
                      %mi v
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \chi_u \Rightarrow \chi_v
              iff
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi w
                      %mo ∩
                      %mi u
                      %mo =
                      %mi w
                      %mo ∩
                      %mi u
                      %mo ∩
                      %mi v
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w \cap u = w \cap u \cap v
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi w
                      %mo ∩
                      %mi u
                      %mo ≤
                      %mi v
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w \cap u \leq v
          .num_cor
            %h6#corollary_2 Corollary
            %p
              In every subobject poset
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Sub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sub(X)
          .proof
            %h6#proof_6 Proof
            %p
              Because
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo ∩
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \cap -
              is left adjoint to the external operator
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo ⇒
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \Rightarrow -
              on
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Sub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sub(X)
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Sub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sub(X)
          %p
            Normally these results are proved in the context of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/toposes"} toposes
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ω
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega
            is an internal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Boolean+algebra"} Boolean algebra
            if and only if the topos is
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Boolean+topos"} Boolean
          %p
            In a topos, the subobject classifier
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ω
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega
            is always
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injective+object"} injective
            %em power object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega^X
            for every object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            (See at
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injective+object#Exponential_injectives"} injective object
            for some of the details). In particular, every object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            embeds into an injective object by the singleton monomorphism
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\to\Omega^X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mi X
